CLICKIT | COMPLETE APPLICATION SPECIFICATION

How to use this specification

This document expands the Clickit project into detailed product requirements for all five connected components. It is intended for product planning, UI/UX design, backend implementation, database design, QA and operational preparation.

Status labels  CONFIRMED = directly discussed in the Clickit project. PROPOSED = recommended product behaviour to validate. FUTURE = useful expansion that should not block the first pilot.

Product definition

Clickit – Home Affairs is a hyperlocal marketplace that connects customers with nearby independent workers and local shops for services such as laundry, tailoring and footwear repair. Workers manage their own digital storefronts, service catalogue, prices and availability. Clickit coordinates discovery, booking, optional pickup and return, payments, support and trust.

Core principle

Product interpretation

Local service marketplace

Clickit helps customers discover and book nearby service providers; it is not a warehouse or grocery dark-store model.

Worker autonomy

Workers control their own catalogue, working hours, capacity and service prices within platform rules.

Choice of fulfilment

A customer may visit the shop, use worker-managed delivery or request Clickit-managed pickup/return where enabled.

Smart Batch

Separate customer orders can share one scheduled route; their booking records and physical parcels remain separate.

One connected platform

Four user-facing clients share one central API/backend and one governed data model.

