1.3 Global interface and accessibility rules

Use the Clickit palette consistently: primary #181A2F, secondary #242E49, slate #37415C, peach #FDA481, red #B4182D and burgundy #54162B.

Use red for destructive actions, urgent failures or important warnings—not for ordinary navigation.

Every data-loading screen needs loading, empty, error and retry states.

Every form needs required-field indication, inline validation and a clear submit result.

Confirm destructive actions such as cancel, delete, reject or refund before committing.

Show currency as INR (₹) and clearly identify whether a price is estimated, worker-confirmed or final.

Do not hide delivery charges, service charges, taxes or discounts inside an unexplained total.

Support accessible text sizes, readable contrast, screen-reader labels and touch targets.

Use local date/time consistently and display time windows with start and end times.

