Collect name and optional email/profile photo if needed. Explain why required fields are needed. Allow later editing.

C06 — Location permission

Explain that location helps find nearby services. Offer allow, choose location manually or skip until discovery requires it.

C07 — Address selection

Search address, map pin, current location or manual entry. Collect house/building, street, landmark, locality, city, postal code and delivery instructions. Save a labelled address.

C08 — Home dashboard

Show selected address, search bar, service categories, nearby providers, popular services, active order card and support entry. Do not show empty promotional placeholders.

C09 — Search

Search services, workers and shop names. Support spelling tolerance and recent searches. Return useful empty state with category suggestions.

C10 — Category listing

Show category description, available services and nearby providers. Filter by distance, rating, price range, open/available status and fulfilment option.

C11 — Map/list results

Show provider cards with business name, service match, distance/ETA where reliable, rating count, indicative price and open status. Map is supplementary; list must remain usable.

C12 — Worker/shop profile

Show verified status, shop name, photos, description, address/service area, hours, services, prices, estimated turnaround, fulfilment options, ratings and policies.

C13 — Service details

Explain what is included/excluded, pricing unit (per cloth, per kg, per item, per alteration, etc.), minimum quantity, expected turnaround and whether final quote may change.

C14 — Booking builder

Select service, quantity/items/weight, item notes, optional photos, fulfilment method, address and requested time. Validate service-specific inputs.

C15 — Fulfilment choice

Offer shop drop-off, worker-managed pickup/return or Clickit pickup/return only where the provider supports it. Show charges and service area.

C16 — Pickup slot selection

Show available windows, capacity and whether a shared batch slot is available. Clearly label a window as estimated or confirmed. Customer must approve a changed slot.

C17 — Booking review

Summarize provider, service, quantity, address, slot, fulfilment, item notes, estimated/confirmed price, delivery fee, tax and total. Require explicit confirmation.

C18 — Booking submitted

Show booking ID and status. Explain that worker confirmation may be pending. Prevent duplicate submission with idempotency.

C19 — Worker quote / clarification

