2.3 Customer booking journey

Customer opens Home and confirms the correct service address.

Customer selects Laundry, Tailoring or Footwear Repair, then chooses a service.

Customer compares local providers using service fit, price, availability, distance and ratings.

Customer opens a provider profile and checks the provider's fulfilment options.

Customer builds a booking with quantity/weight/item notes and chooses a slot.

If a shared pickup route is available, customer sees the pickup window and chooses it voluntarily.

Customer reviews the price breakdown and submits the booking.

Worker accepts or requests clarification; customer confirms any revised quote.

Customer completes payment according to the configured payment policy.

Customer follows pickup, service and return milestones; customer can raise a support case at any point.

After successful receipt, booking completes and customer may rate the service.

2.4 Customer-specific business rules

Never confirm a worker, price or slot before the backend has reserved/confirmed it.

Show the price unit next to every price. ₹10 per cloth is not the same as ₹10 per kg or per order.

Show the distinction between estimated price and final confirmed price.

Require approval before charging for a changed scope or additional item.

Do not automatically place a customer into a shared batch if the slot or fee changes from what they accepted.

Do not show another customer's name, address, order ID or parcel details in batch tracking.

Allow a customer to contact support without needing to understand internal batch or dispatch identifiers.

