4.3 Delivery partner rules

Partner sees only active assigned task information and the minimum necessary personal data.

Partner location tracking is active only for a disclosed operational purpose and limited to active work/online periods.

Partner cannot change service price, booking item count or worker earnings.

Partner cannot mark pickup/drop complete without required verification and custody event.

Partner may reject unsafe or impossible work without penalty rules being hidden.

Batch offers must display total capacity requirements and stop count before acceptance.

Reassignment preserves the old assignment record and records why it ended.

4.4 Smart Batch behaviour in partner app

A batch is a route plan containing multiple separate stops. It is not one combined customer order. The partner sees a route summary and then each stop independently.

Batch action

Required behaviour

Offer

Show time window, route estimate, total parcel count/weight estimate, capacity and payout.

Accept

Reserve the batch assignment atomically; reject duplicate acceptance.

Start route

Record start time and show stop order.

At each stop

Verify correct booking/parcel, record proof and mark only that stop complete.

Partial failure

Skip or flag the affected stop; other completed stops remain completed.

Re-route

Operations may reorder remaining stops or reassign remaining work with an audit record.

Close batch

Close only when all stops are completed or explicitly resolved as exceptions.

