6.2 API conventions

Version endpoints under /api/v1.

Use HTTPS and JSON with consistent response envelopes and error codes.

Validate every request server-side; do not trust client-calculated prices, permissions, statuses or coordinates.

Use pagination, filtering and sorting for list endpoints.

Use idempotency keys for booking creation, payment initiation and retry-sensitive commands.

Use optimistic concurrency or transactions for worker acceptance, slot reservation, batch capacity and assignment.

Verify payment webhooks with provider signatures and deduplicate provider event IDs.

Return only the fields appropriate to the authenticated role and object relationship.

Use structured logs with request IDs while scrubbing secrets, OTPs, payment data and unnecessary personal information.

